--==============================================================================================
-- Wind Leaves & Atmosphere script
-- Original Author: Daedalus-Prime
-- EXPEDITION WEATHERS EDIT
-- Edited by FabioConte for Stalker Anomaly Seasons (01/03/2023)
-- Edited by Hippobot for Stalker Anomaly: Atmospherics Version 1.54++
-- Edited by Grok 09/03/2023, actor_on_update optimisation and map restrictions

-- Edited by Ivan Danko
-- Reworked: presets from dynamic_weather_graphs.ltx, time-of-day logic
-- Fixed: cleanup, memory optimization, position comparison - 2025
-- Fixes:
--   1. stop_deffered -> stop() (method does not exist in xray-monolith)
--   2. vector():set(0,0,0) removed from the loop
--   3. move_to throttle — only when the actor is actually moving
--   4. particles_object wrapped in pcall (protection against crashes if the file is not found)
--   5. alife()/game_graph() are cached — the level is not recalculated every 100 ms
--   6. db.actor is checked before use
--   7. Cleanup added when unloading the level
--   8. Optimised movement check via distance_to_sqr
--   9. Fixed weather check for nil
--   10. Added logging of particle loading errors
--   11. Fallback for is_underground via leaves_maps
--   12. Fixed %d crash with nil — replaced with tostring()
--   13. DEBUG log moved to snowfall() to ensure printing
--   14. Underground: 3x fogdust_00 + 1x nature\fog_foggy_00
--   15. BUGFIX: Removed hud_mode (true) from play_at_pos for underground particles —
--       in hud_mode, the position is interpreted in the HUD camera space, not the world space,
--       so particles were launched out of sight. Now all particles play
--       in the world space at the actor's position.
--   16. BUGFIX: play_or_move_ug merged with play_or_move — unified logic.
--   17. Added p_foggdust_00 (nature\effects\exp_pfx_foggdust_00) and
--       p_fog_dirt (nature\effects\fog_foggy_dirt) — in dungeons and rooms.
--   18. PERF: Removed pcall closure from level_check hot path — closure allocation
--       caused GC pressure and microfreezes on LuaJIT. Replaced with safe nil-checks.
--       vertex_id cached — level_name() called only when vertex actually changes.
--   19. PERF: play_underground converted to flat array — ipairs instead of pairs,
--       no hash table overhead per tick.
--   20. PERF: stop_all_except rewritten — single pass, no double iteration.
--   21. PERF: LOGIC_INTERVAL 500->1000ms, MOVE_INTERVAL 200->500ms —
--       weather/fog changes are imperceptible at 1s granularity,
--       particle position updates at 500ms are invisible to the player.
-- Dead Zone edit:
--   22. snowfall(): constant atmospheric fog outdoors regardless of weather cycle —
--       p_fogdust_00 (nature\exp_pfx_fogdust_00). Anthology v138 removes the second
--       fullscreen p_fog_light layer because it duplicated the same outdoor fog role.
--       Added to active{} first, before any weather-dependent logic.
--   23. Presets in cycle_* tables verified against dynamic_weather_graphs.ltx:
--       cycle_clear(14), cycle_partly(14), cycle_cloudy(20), cycle_rain(13),
--       cycle_storm(11), cycle_foggy(10). w_ccgim_original excluded (commented out in .ltx).
--   24. grimwood/promzona/poselok_ug already present in leaves_maps as surface maps (=1).
-- Summer edit:
--   25. Summer time-of-day constants: night fog 01-03, leaves 18-21, insects 9-20.
--   26. Added p_leaves_calm (nature\exp_pfx_leaves_calm) — calm daytime leaves outdoors.
--   27. Added p_flies (nature\flies_01) — midges/insects during daytime, clear/cloudy weather.
--   28. Added p_fog_night (nature\exp_pfx_fog_night) — dedicated night fog preset.
--   29. Added p_storm_dust (nature\effects\fog_stormy_dust) — dust storm during storm weather.
--   30. Added p_storm_leaves (nature\effects\fog_stormy_leaves_01) — storm leaves.
--   31. Distant tornado during storm: rare, random, within map boundaries, no sound.
--       Architecture mirrors distant_storm in level_weathers — position beyond actor
--       sight distance, boundary check. Particles: fog_tornado_00, fog_tornado_01 —
--       one random per spawn. Timer: every 3-8 in-game minutes, 40% chance.
-- Optimization edit:
--   32. PERF: cached_weather + cached_hour — snowfall() is skipped if weather, hour
--       and position have not changed. Primary gain: stop_all_except over 19 particles
--       every second replaced with no-op on the majority of ticks.
--   33. PERF: cached_time_factor — level.get_time_factor() cached for 5 real seconds
--       instead of being called on every get_diff_sec() invocation.
--   34. PERF: tornado_vec — single reused vector() for tornado spawn position;
--       no new object allocated per spawn.
-- mt_particles fix:
--   35. BUGFIX: All particles_object method calls (stop/play_at_pos/move_to) are now
--       deferred via a pending queue and flushed through CreateTimeEvent(delay=1).
--       delay=1 (one in-game second) guarantees CParticlesAsync has exited UpdateSpatial
--       before the flush runs, eliminating the ISpatial_DB::remove race condition
--       (Access violation c0000005 at AnomalyDX11AVX!ISpatial_DB::remove+0x34).
--       Each CreateTimeEvent uses a unique key (wl_flush_N) to prevent silent drops
--       when schedule_flush() is called again before the previous event fires.
--       Each op in flush_pending is wrapped in pcall to isolate residual errors
--       without aborting the rest of the queue.
--       on_game_unload stop() calls use immediate stop_p_immediate() — at that point
--       CParticlesAsync is already shut down by the engine.
--==============================================================================================

